 - Inlines the runtime from its own folder, once. It never inlines media: each local `src` on `img`, `video`, `audio`, `source` or `doc-shot` stays a literal path, and the plans CLI uploads the file when it publishes the page. That file must sit in the page's own folder, never only under `--root`, and be an image or video type in the `plans:publish` table. A page holds at most 64 such files. pack reads a `src` as the CLI does: `&amp;` and numeric references decode, and any other `&name;` is refused, so write the character itself. `data:` URIs pass.
